{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1498289-the-realm-defense-grid","id":1498289,"title":"The Realm Defense Grid","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-29T04:44:40-08:00","id":1498289,"title":"The Realm Defense Grid","content":"So the Empress walked into the Imperial Mance, activated the Sword of Creation and nuked the Fair Folk from orbit, just to be sure.<br /> <br /> Why did she stop there?<br /> <br /> Why did she undertake several unsuccessful attacks on the Scavenger Lands, when all she needed to do was wipe Lookshy off the map and march her Legions into the less-defended remnants?<br /> <br /> Is there some official metaplot mystery regarding this or is this a plot hole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T15:26:32-07:00","id":1522644,"title":"","content":"Well, one of the side effects of the Sword of Creation is that it produces disasters on its wake. On the Balorian Crusade it makes sense. Who cares about some drownings and earthquakes when the Creation itself was safe? But it would be kinda useless to destroy Lookshy and drown the Neck for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T19:49:49-07:00","id":1522654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSteve2020</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1498289-the-realm-defense-grid#post1498289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Empress walked into the Imperial Mance, activated the Sword of Creation and nuked the Fair Folk from orbit, just to be sure.<br /> <br /> Why did she stop there?<br /> <br /> Why did she undertake several unsuccessful attacks on the Scavenger Lands, when all she needed to do was wipe Lookshy off the map and march her Legions into the less-defended remnants?<br /> <br /> Is there some official metaplot mystery regarding this or is this a plot hole?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2nd edition at least it stated that activating the Realm Defense Grid causes massive earthquakes and aftershocks on the Imperial Isle. Sure she could blow up Lookshy, but she would also inflict untold devastation to her own territories. The Sword of Creation is basically a weapon of last resort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T20:54:00-07:00","id":1522655,"title":"","content":"The idea of backlash against the Blessed Isle was a much later addition yes, and I go back and forth on whether or not it adds value.<br /> <br /> As far as using it to destroy the Scavenger Lands, the original depiction has one stated reason and one that I think is readily inferred.<br /> <br /> The former is that the area around Lookshy is supposed to be very close to an extremely sensitive geomantic construct that is powering the River of Tears, and being destroyed by something like the Sword of Creation would unleash catastrophic amounts of energy that is currently carefully balanced.<br /> <br /> The latter would be in the fact that destroying the Scavenger Lands so thoroughly rather defeats the purpose of wanting to make war on it in the first place. Like, it's an area filled with significant trade hubs, lots of high quality arable land, and a few stockpiles of treasures from the First Age. You fight for the sake of ensuring that all of that stuff will come under your control and contribute to your wealth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, but isn't the war as a response to the fact that they're being all defiant?&quot;<br /> <br /> The whole reason that the defiance is a problem is because it means they're not paying tribute.<br /> <br /> They're not some threat to national security or anything; they don't particularly have the means to make war on the Realm on their own turf, and even if they managed to assemble a navy that could be a genuine meaningful threat, <i>that</i> is something you can shoot the Defence Grid at.<br /> <br /> (I've seen some arguments that there was an intended subtext that the extent of the Empress's control over the Grid was less absolute than the propaganda of the Realm would portray, and so behind all sorts of plausible excuses there would be an element of being sparing with it lest it do something like shake off her command, run out of some resource powering it, or have some important system burn out that she could not restore. Even then, that's more a concern about the long term viability for wielding it against Fair Folk hordes that are getting too close to the choice satrapies and have gotten through the legions.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T00:09:11-07:00","id":1522661,"title":"","content":"The earthquakes and stuff are in 3e as well. Though the difference in presentation matters a bit. In 2e it is implied to be a result because she's a Dragon-Blood. It's kind of just a general part of the trend of &quot;Dragon-Blooded suck at using or doing things&quot; of the edition.<br /> <br /> 3e to me indicates more like...that's just how the thing works. And that due to not having the infrastrucutre to fix it if it breaks something (since big complicated machine) means she was judicious in using it. Which didn't mean she wasn't willing to. It just meant that some day it could just snap, and she'd rather that be a future her problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T21:46:08-07:00","id":1522776,"title":"","content":"You don't nuke the farmlands you want producing grain for you, or the jade mines whose bounty you want. The Scavenger Lands aren't an existential threat to the Realm's existence, but they are a highly bountiful region of valuable production. That means seizing the area is worth more than scorching it black. That's even before you get into the horrific side effects of using the Sword of Creation, which have been mentioned upthread as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T13:04:55-07:00","id":1522854,"title":"","content":"I suspect it was probably something she didn't want to do on a personal level since that would just have made her come off as just another person who picked up a ridiculously powerful tool/trick and over extended themselves trying to gobble up territory. Whereas her proclamation, at least in the 3e story, amounts to saying she's the most qualified because she has the best ability to protect people.<br /> <br /> Essentially using the imperial manse would easily help her expand territory by crushing her foes, but well damage to the areas means more work would have been needed. At least in the earlier days I think she was probably doing the smarter move of consolidating her own power base than trying to expand out rapidly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T14:39:59-07:00","id":1524369,"title":"","content":"Another consideration for those who are thinking of a potential juicy reveal for their campaigns... Is that the Empress couldn't use the Sword of Creation. Though if I remember from a 1e or 2e project, she had used it again on the 5 Tiger Generals or something. Maybe the aftermath of that wasn't worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}